@startuml
title Population, samples and the sampling distribution of the mean
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam rectangle {
  BackgroundColor #EAF6F0
  BorderColor #2E8B67
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  BorderColor #2E8B67
}
rectangle "Population (N ~ 422,000 daily highs)\nmean mu ~ 16.3 C, SD sigma ~ 9.44 C" as P
rectangle "Sample 1 (n values)\nmean x1, SD s1" as S1
rectangle "Sample 2 (n values)\nmean x2, SD s2" as S2
rectangle "Sample k (n values)\nmean xk, SD sk" as Sk
rectangle "Sampling distribution of the mean\ncentre ~ mu, SD = SE = sigma / sqrt(n)\napproximately normal (CLT)" as D
rectangle "One-sample estimate\nSE_hat = s / sqrt(n)\n95 % CI = x +/- 1.96 SE_hat" as E
P --> S1 : random.sample
P --> S2 : random.sample
P --> Sk : random.sample
S1 --> D
S2 --> D
Sk --> D
S1 --> E : in practice only one sample exists
D ..> E : theory says what SE is
note right of D
  more samples: same SD of means
  larger n: SD shrinks as 1/sqrt(n)
end note
@enduml
